   "subject": "High transect predictions when including covariates INLABRU",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Apologies for the long\r\nemail, I have tried to include all the potentially relevant details of this issue.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">We have multiple </span>season<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">s of survey data. We do not want to include a\r\ntemporal effect between </span>seasons<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">. We wish\r\nto treat each </span>season<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> as an independent\r\nreplicate.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">We would like to build a\r\nLGCP model to generate spatial predictions, and assess the effect of a number\r\nof environmental covariates.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">We wish to use an SPDE to\r\naccount for spatial autocorrelations not accounted for by environmental\r\ncovariates. The ideal scenario would so that the output of an SPDE only model,\r\nand a model with multiple covariates would be similar, and we could assess the\r\nindependent contributions of spatial covariates.<u></u><u></u></span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><br></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Our transects are 0.9km wide\r\nwith a 5km spacing. We do not have distance data for the samples.<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Firstly we built a LGCP\r\nmodel as follows:<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">max.edge &lt;-\r\nmax(round(diff(range(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> @coords[,1]))/20),\r\nround(diff(range(rbind(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">\r\n@coords[,2]))/20)))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">## max.edge = 15<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">bound.outer =\r\nmax(round(diff(range(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> @coords[,1]))),\r\nround(diff(range(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> @coords[,2]))))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">## bound.outer = 250<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">my.boundary &lt;- gBuffer(my.transects,\r\nwidth = 10, byid = F)<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">mesh = inla.mesh.2d(max.edge\r\n= c(1,5)*max.edge,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                     boundary = my.boundary,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                     cutoff = 1, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                     offset = c(max.edge * 5,\r\nbound.outer),<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                     crs = inla.CRS(projargs =\r\nCRS(proj4string(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">)))) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">pcmatern &lt;-\r\ninla.spde2.pcmatern(mesh, <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                                    alpha = 2,<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                                    prior.sigma\r\n= c(0.01, 0.01), <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">                                    prior.range\r\n= c(20, 0.05))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Season &lt;-</span> point.data$<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Season</span><u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">nseas &lt;- length(unique(</span>point.data<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">$Season)) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">mdl.components<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"> &lt;- ~\r\nspat(map = coordinates, group = Season, ngroup = nseas, model = pcmatern,\r\ncontrol.group = list(model = &quot;iid&quot;))<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">my.transects$weight &lt;-\r\n0.9<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">ips &lt;- ipoints(my.transects,\r\nmesh, group = &quot;Season&quot;) <u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">fit.model.spde &lt;- inlabru::lgcp(components = mdl.components,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                                 data = point.data,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                                 ips = ips,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                                 formula =\r\nmdl.formula,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                                 options =\r\nlist(control.compute = list(dic = TRUE,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                         \r\n                                             waic\r\n= TRUE,<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">                                                                      \r\nconfig = TRUE)))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">This model seems to work ok. When using the model to predict\r\nthe intensity for integration points along our transects for each season, the\r\ntotal predictions for each season are similar to what we have observed. The\r\ntotal estimate of points across the entire survey area is also similar to what\r\nwe would expect.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">ips.t.1 = subset(ips,ips$<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Season</span>\r\n== 1)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">ips.t.2 = subset(ips,ips$<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Season</span>\r\n== 2)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">ips.t.3 = subset(ips,ips$<span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Season</span>\r\n== 3)<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">total.1 = predict(fit.model.spde, ips.t.1, ~ sum(weight *\r\nexp(spat + Intercept)))<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">We then added 5 spatial covariates. Each covariate was\r\nmodelled as a linear response.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">These values were extracted for both the integration points “ips”,\r\nand the point data “point.data” before\r\nrunning the lgcp model and stored within the dataframe attached to “point.data”.\r\nEach point’s covariate value was centred by the mean value across the entire\r\nmesh extent. The values were returned during lgcp() and predict() by defining a series of\r\nfunctions. <u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">We then compared 6 separate models by dropping one covariate\r\nat a time. The most complex models generally had lower WAIC and DIC scores. The\r\ncoeffients of each spatial covariate did not overlap with zero in any case.<u></u><u></u></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The problem is that when covariates are included, the intensity predictions at integration\r\npoints along our transects are far higher\r\nthan what we would expect. The predictions across the entire survey region are\r\nalso far higher.<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">I am suspicious that the reason for this result could be due\r\nto the construction of the pcmatern? </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Or perhaps I have misspecified something\r\nwithin the code? </p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Our transects preferentially sample more suitable areas so this may also present issues when we interpret our covariates<u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Any guidance here would be appreciated. <u></u><u></u></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><br></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\">Many thanks</p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\"><u></u> <u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"font-size:10pt;line-height:107%;font-family:Arial,sans-serif;background-image:initial;background-position:initial;background-size:initial;background-repeat:initial;background-origin:initial;background-clip:initial\">Feng<u></u><u></u></span></p>\r\n\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><u></u> <u></u></p></div>"
    ]
   ]
  }
 ]
}
